ternal beam radiation and /or chemotherapy with temozolamide.\n2. Women who were pregnant, breast feeding, or possibly pregnant.\n3. Patients with hepatic or renal dysfunction.\n4. Patients with MRI contraindications (i.e. pacemakers, non-MR compatible devices).\n5. Patients with a history of drug hypersensitivity to 18F-Fluciclovine.\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "AND": {\n                    "left": {\n                      "raw_text": "1. Patient diagnosis with glioma but before surgery, external beam radiation",\n                      "Procedure": [\n                        "surgery",\n                        "external beam radiation"\n                      ],\n                      "Procedure-Name": [\n                        "surgery",\n                        "external beam radiation"\n                      ],\n                      "Condition": [\n                        "glioma"\n                      ],\n                      "Condition-Name": [\n                        "glioma"\n                      ],\n                      "Modifier": [\n                        "before"\n                      ]\n                    },\n                    "right": {\n                      "raw_text": "and /or chemotherapy with temozolamide.",\n                      "Procedure": [\n                        "chemotherapy"\n                      ],\n                      "Procedure-Name": [\n                        "chemotherapy"\n                      ],\n                      "Drug": [\n                        "temozolamide"\n                      ],\n                      "Drug-Name": [\n                        "temozolamide"\n                      ]\n                    }\n                  }\n                },\n                "right": {\n                  "OR": {\n                    "left": {\n         