severe growth retardation with Doppler abnormalities, fetal malformation or a known fetal genetic defect.\n-  Anomaly of placental adhesion.\n-  Caesarean in a context of medical or obstetric emergency.\n-  Caesarean section performed under general anesthesia following failure of locoregional anesthesia.\n-  Refusal of the woman to participate in the study.\n-  Impossibility or failure to study the neonatal acid-base balance on the umbilical cord.\n\n### Response:\n{\n  "AND": {\n    "left": {\n      "AND": {\n        "left": {\n          "AND": {\n            "left": {\n              "AND": {\n                "left": {\n                  "AND": {\n                    "left": {\n                      "OR": {\n                        "left": {\n                          "raw_text": "- Fetal pathology known prenatally like intrauterine severe growth retardation",\n                          "Condition": [\n                            "intrauterine severe growth retardation",\n                            "pathology"\n                          ],\n                          "Condition-Name": [\n                            "intrauterine severe growth retardation",\n                            "pathology"\n                          ],\n                          "Modifier": [\n                            "Fetal",\n                            "prenatally"\n                          ],\n                          "Severity": [\n                            "severe"\n                          ]\n                        },\n                        "right": {\n                          "raw_text": "with Doppler abnormalities, fetal malformation or a known fetal genetic defect.",\n                          "Condition": [\n                            "malformation",\n                            "Doppler abnormalities",\n                            "fetal genetic defect"\n                          ],\n                          "Condition-Name": [\n                            "malformation",\n                            "Doppler abnormalities",\n                            "fetal genetic defect"\n                          ],\n                          "Modifier": [\n                            "fetal"\n                          ]\n                        }\n                      }\n                    },\n                    "right": {\n                      "raw_text": "- Anomaly of placental adhesion.",\n                      "Condition": [\n                        "placental adhesion"\n                      ],\n                      "Condition-Name": [\n                        "placental adhesion"\n                      ],\n                      "Modifier": [\n                        "Anomaly"\n                      ]\n                    }\n                  }\n                },\n                "right": {\n                  "OR": {\n                    "left": {\n                      "raw_text": "- Caesarean in a context of medical",\n                      "Procedure": [\n                        "Caesarean"\n                      ],\n                      "Procedure-Name": [\n                        "Caesarean"\n                      ],\n                      "Modifier": [\n                        "medical"\n                      ]\n                    },\n                    "right": {\n                      "raw_text": "or obstetric emergency.",\n                      "Modifier": [\n                        "obstetric"\n                      ],\n                      "Encounter": [\n                        "emergency"\n                      ]\n                    }\n                  }\n                }\n              }\n            },\n            "right": {\n              "raw_text": "- Caesarean section performed under general anesthesia following failure of locoregional anesthesia.",\n              "Procedure": [\n                "general anesthesia",\n                "Caesarean section",\n                "locoregional anesthesia"\n 